@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;recovery] namespace-sweep-privilege-scope
The helper MUST run in PID 1's mount namespace and requires CAP_SYS_ADMIN in
the initial user namespace; it is never setuid. Only ordinary unmounts of the
exact ZFS root at the canonical path are allowed; aliases, nested mounts,
unreadable inventories, live users and detected races fail closed. It never
forces, lazily detaches, kills a process or exposes path diagnostics: stdout
carries exactly one fixed outcome line consumed by Lilly.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] namespace-unmount-hegel-properties
Hegel properties MUST cover the dataset/path validators and their shared
character class over arbitrary bytes, octal mount-field decoding, mountinfo
classification (exact/alias/descendant/duplicate/malformed) and sweep plan
dedup/caps. Namespace-entering and real unmount authority remain with the
disposable NixOS storage fixtures that drive production cleanup paths.
